{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And after saying \"two\"</b>, he clarified that they shall be male and female. And after stating a general rule — \"of all that lives, of all flesh\" — he then specified: of the fowl after its kind, of the beast after its kind, and of every creeping thing that is upon the earth — this is a general rule for the beasts of the field. And likewise \"small and great,\" that which is born from male and female; and there are excluded all that are born without joining of two. So too the creatures of the water, for even the fish is called flesh — proof is what Moses said: <b>\"And you said, 'I will give them flesh,' the sheep and the cattle, etc., if all the fish of the sea\"</b> (Numbers 11:21–22)." "<b>And the word 'you shall bring into the ark'</b> is a command upon Noah that he not abandon them, but rather bring them with him, to keep seed alive of every kind."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved the closing citation reference to Numbers 11:21–22 based on the quoted phrases matching both verses."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:36.319310808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}